From 3aa59457f088af12f60048ba69819dbe33ac99e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:44:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(update): show backup progress and clone state.db before
 a Desktop update [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Desktop's emergency state.db backup before a client update copied the
whole database (21.7 GB on one machine: ~2 min) and then ran PRAGMA
quick_check on the copy (5+ more min, deaf to SIGTERM), while the update
overlay said "Getting ready… Starting update…" over a bar that never moved.

hermes_cli/backup_sqlite.py (script run):
- Copy-on-write clone first: BEGIN IMMEDIATE on state.db, clone state.db and
  its -wal (macOS clonefile(2), Linux ioctl FICLONE on btrfs/xfs), release the
  lock, then verify the clone (SQLite header, opens, schema_version reads,
  its WAL checkpointed back into one file). No full check: under the write
  lock the clone is the committed bytes. The lock waits at most 2 s and is
  never held across the fallback; result carries method and lock_ms.
- Any clone failure (EXDEV/ENOTSUP/EOPNOTSUPP, held lock, bad clone) falls
  back to the existing page copy, which now reports progress and announces
  its quick_check, which runs off the main thread so SIGTERM stops it.
- Progress is one JSON object per stderr line, at most two a second plus a
  final 100% line: {"event":"backup_progress","done_bytes","total_bytes",
  "method"} and {"event":"backup_check"}. stdout still carries only the
  result object. HERMES_PREFLIGHT_CLONE=0 turns the clone off.

Desktop:
- state-db-preflight spawns the snapshot and parses stderr as it arrives
  (lines split across chunks, garbage ignored); other stderr lines go to the
  log and into the failure message.
- The checkout strategy forwards it on the existing update-progress channel
  as stage "backup" (percent = done/total, backup {phase, bytes, method});
  the Windows "this window will close" stage now follows the backup.
- The overlay shows "Backing up your chat history before updating: 12.3 of
  21.7 GB" with a determinate bar, then "Checking the backup…".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
